The <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a> does not include an Action Button, according to the device's <a href="https://www.apple.com/iphone-duo/specs/">technical specifications page</a>. The page's diagram highlights volume up/down buttons at the top, Camera Control and side buttons on the right side, a USB-C port at the bottom, and microphones and speakers at the top and bottom.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/iphone-duo-no-action-button.jpg" alt="" width="1263" height="710" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1063591" /><br/>
On the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-18-pro/">iPhone 18 Pro</a> models and earlier, the Action Button is located on the left side of the iPhone right above the volume up/down buttons.<br/>
<br/>
The Action Button is a customizable button that can be assigned one of several actions. It can do things like activate Silent mode (the default), set a Focus, turn on the Flashlight, record a Voice Memo, activate <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/visual-intelligence/">Visual Intelligence</a>, or run a Shortcut.<br/>
<br/>
Apple introduced the Action Button with the iPhone 15 Pro, and all iPhones released since then have included the feature. The &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; is the first iPhone that has no option for a physical mute toggle. Silent mode will need to be turned on via Control Center.<br/>
<br/>
